<title>USA: Reynolds Metals completes sale of plant.</title>
<headline>Reynolds Metals completes sale of plant.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reynolds Metals Co said Monday said it has completed the sale of its aluminum reclamation plant in Bellwood, Va., to Philip Environmental Inc, of Hamilton, Ontario.</p>
<p>The plant has about 100 employees, all of whom have been offered employment by Philip, Reynolds Metals said.</p>
<p>The plant is a secondary recycling facility that processes scrap aluminum into a deoxidizing agent used by the steel industry.</p>
<p>Reynolds Metals said the deal is part of its previously announced portfolio review and will not have a material effect on its second quarter results.</p>
</text>
